{"lines": ["Four cases. Each one has an owl, or another bird, standing next to it.", "Notice the careful word. Proposed. Not proven.", "Brian Dunning thinks the Dover answer is ordinary. But he also asks why a snowy owl would fool several people in one town within a day, when, he says, that illusion never fooled anyone before or since. He adds that he is not calling the kids liars.", "So here is the honest version. Known: sincere witnesses reported glowing eyes in the dark. Proposed: owls, herons, a crane, a meteor, a truck. Unsolved: why the same few shapes, again and again.", "Do not pretend you know more than you do, in either direction."], "words": [["Four", 0.0, 0.2], ["cases.", 0.2, 0.5], ["Each", 0.98, 1.14], ["one", 1.14, 1.34], ["has", 1.34, 1.5], ["an", 1.5, 1.64], ["owl,", 1.64, 1.96], ["or", 1.96, 2.3], ["another", 2.3, 2.6], ["bird,", 2.6, 2.92], ["standing", 2.92, 3.3], ["next", 3.3, 3.76], ["to", 3.76, 3.94], ["it.", 3.94, 4.1], ["Notice", 4.68, 5.04], ["the", 5.04, 5.26], ["careful", 5.26, 5.48], ["word.", 5.48, 5.96], ["Proposed.", 6.24, 6.48], ["Not", 6.48, 6.96], ["proven.", 6.96, 7.28], ["Brian", 8.2, 8.58], ["Dunning", 8.58, 8.94], ["thinks", 8.94, 9.36], ["the", 9.36, 9.52], ["Dover", 9.52, 9.72], ["answer", 9.72, 10.22], ["is", 10.22, 10.56], ["ordinary.", 10.56, 11.06], ["But", 11.68, 11.9], ["he", 11.9, 11.98], ["also", 11.98, 12.22], ["asks", 12.22, 12.72], ["why", 12.72, 13.02], ["a", 13.02, 13.2], ["snowy", 13.2, 13.46], ["owl", 13.46, 14.08], ["would", 14.08, 14.38], ["fool", 14.38, 14.62], ["several", 14.62, 15.08], ["people", 15.08, 15.56], ["in", 15.56, 15.82], ["one", 15.82, 15.98], ["town", 15.98, 16.32], ["within", 16.32, 16.62], ["a", 16.62, 16.84], ["day,", 16.84, 17.1], ["when,", 17.1, 17.38], ["he", 17.38, 17.76], ["says,", 17.76, 18.06], ["that", 18.06, 18.56], ["illusion", 18.56, 18.86], ["never", 18.86, 19.36], ["fooled", 19.36, 19.68], ["anyone", 19.68, 20.14], ["before", 20.14, 20.66], ["or", 20.66, 20.98], ["since.", 20.9